{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"79916c9dfb3339be8ca16b95287a45a2051ea73fbc26bbc992699f5fcadec17c","digest":{"component_or_area":"claude-skills testing infrastructure and documentation","key_entities":["examples/claude-skills/shared/test-design.md","examples/claude-skills/rebar-debug/test-design.md","examples/claude-skills/rebar-implement/test-design.md","examples/claude-skills/rebar-brainstorm/test-design.md","tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py","examples/claude-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md","examples/claude-skills/rebar-debug/llm-behavioral-taxonomy.md","examples/claude-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md","examples/claude-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md","examples/claude-skills/README.md"],"problem_keywords":["test design","TDD","RED oracle","contract card","test tier","shared standard","drift gating","byte-identical copies"],"propositions":["The shared test-design.md canonical file does not exist; it must be authored with coverage of RED oracle inventory, contract card structure, test-tier selection rules, oracle minimums, fault realism, gating proof, and defect-seeded mutation.","Three consuming skills (rebar-debug, rebar-implement, rebar-brainstorm) lack byte-identical copies of the standard, preventing unified test guidance and drift-gated consistency.","No drift-gating unit test enforces byte-identity of test-design.md copies across skill directories, allowing silent divergence of the shared standard.","rebar-debug SKILL.md Step 4 does not explicitly address RED oracle design with coverage inventory and contract card before test authoring.","rebar-debug Step 5 does not hand the fixer a frozen contract card alongside root cause and reproduction steps.","rebar-implement and rebar-brainstorm lack explicit directives to apply the shared test-design standard during acceptance-criteria planning and oracle authoring."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2